OL,3,AWe couldn't afford a house alone, so we
OL,4,Abought one with strangers
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Elizabeth and Tom Wilcox realised
OL,7,Fthey could never afford to buy the home
OL,8,Fthey wanted for themselves and their
OL,9,Ftwo children, they decided to take a
OL,10,Fleap of faith.
OL,12,FThey'd find another couple with young
OL,13,Fkids, complete strangers to them, and
OL,14,Fpropose that they go halves on a
OL,15,Fproperty and all move in together.
OL,17,FBased in Vancouver, which has long had
OL,18,Fsome of the highest house prices in
OL,19,FCanada, the Wilcoxes were desperate to
OL,20,Fbuy a home that had a back garden for
OL,21,Ftheir children to play in.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
